# The private tier. Everything here is tracked on `local` and pushed to the
# private origin, and is stripped by tools/release.ts before master is cut, so
# it never reaches the public repository. One .gitignore for both tiers; this
# is the second, tighter list the release applies. Prefixes, one per line.
notes/
packages/mining/
# The per-instrument WAV export (Eugene, 09-22): his, for wave analysis, and
# never public; and since 09-25 (record-r1) the whole theme as a WAV and the
# ring as a video, the record row under the ledger's title, never public either.
# Loaded only behind __PRIVATE_TOOLS__; tools/check-release.ts holds the shipped
# files to never naming the folder's modules anywhere else and to never carrying
# the mark each of them stamps into itself.
packages/deep-house/src/machine/private/
mining/
# The keys lab (round LIQUID-KEYS, 10-10): his listening page for picking keys
# tones, spaces and progressions; it reads the unapproved rows in notes/.
packages/deep-house/lab/keys/
# The Apple app (round apple-0, 10-19): the shell for iPhone, iPad and Mac
# that bundles the release site. Private tier until it ships through the store.
apple/
# The promo reel (10-31): a square film of the ring cut from several tracks for
# a post; it renders tracks to video and writes nothing a listener needs, so it
# stays in the private tier with the recorder it drives.
packages/deep-house/tools/promo-reel.ts
# and its films (11-03): each cut list in promo/<name>/reel.json, kept in git so
